<ul class="enc-list"><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/old-smyrna"><span class="enc-name">Old Smyrna</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Old Smyrna is the archaeological site of the first city of Smyrna, on the mound of Tepekule at Bayraklı on the north-eastern shore of the Gulf of Izmir, Turkey.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/old-town-square-prague"><span class="enc-name">Old Town Square</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Old Town Square is the main square of Prague's Old Town, a market place since the twelfth century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/old-turkic"><span class="enc-name">Old Turkic</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Old Turkic is the earliest recorded Turkic language, written in a runic script from the 8th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/old-university-of-leuven"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/old-university-of-leuven.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Old University of Leuven</span><span class="enc-type">Institution</span><span class="enc-snip">The Old University of Leuven was founded in 1425 by Pope Martin V at the request of Duke John IV of Brabant and became one of the great universities of Catholic Europe.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/old-uyghur-language"><span class="enc-name">Old Uyghur language</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Old Uyghur was the Turkic language of the Uyghur Kingdom of Qocho and the Gansu Uyghurs from the 9th to the 14th centuries.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/old-zurich-war.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Old Zürich War</span><span class="enc-type">War · 1440–1446</span><span class="enc-snip">The Old Zürich War was a conflict within the Swiss Confederacy over the inheritance of the last count of Toggenburg, who died in 1436.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ole-romer"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/ole-romer.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ole Rømer</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ole Rømer was a Danish astronomer who in 1676, working at the Paris Observatory, showed from the timing of eclipses of Jupiter's moon Io that light travels at a finite…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oleg-ii-of-ryazan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/oleg-ii-of-ryazan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Oleg II of Ryazan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Oleg II of Ryazan, known as Oleg Ivanovich, was Grand Prince of Ryazan for most of the period from 1350 to 1402.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oleg-of-novgorod"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/oleg-of-novgorod.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Oleg of Novgorod</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Oleg of Novgorod was a Varangian prince who, according to the Primary Chronicle, succeeded Rurik at Novgorod and in 882 seized Kiev, killing its rulers Askold and Dir.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/oleg-sviatoslavich"><span class="enc-name">Oleg Sviatoslavich</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Oleg Sviatoslavich was a Rurikid prince, son of Sviatoslav II of Kiev and ancestor of the Olgovichi princes of Chernigov.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olelkovich"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olelkovich.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olelkovich</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Olelkovich were a princely family of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania, descended from Olelko (Alexander) Vladimirovich, a grandson of Grand Duke Algirdas.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olesnica"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olesnica.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Oleśnica</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Oleśnica is a town in Lower Silesia, Poland, east of Wrocław.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olga-of-kiev"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olga-of-kiev.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olga of Kiev</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Olga was the wife of Prince Igor of Kiev and regent of Kievan Rus' for her son Sviatoslav after Igor's death in 945.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oliba"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/oliba.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Oliba</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Oliba was a Catalan churchman, a son of the count of Cerdanya, who became abbot of Ripoll and Cuixà in 1008 and bishop of Vic in 1018.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olinda"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olinda.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olinda</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Olinda is a colonial town on the coast of Pernambuco, Brazil, founded in 1535 by the donatary Duarte Coelho as the capital of his captaincy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olite"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olite.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olite</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Olite is a town in Navarre, Spain, south of Pamplona.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/olive-oil"><span class="enc-name">Olive oil</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Olive oil is the oil pressed from olives, a staple of Mediterranean diet, lighting and trade since antiquity.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/oliver-cromwell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Oliver Cromwell</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Oliver Cromwell was an English soldier and politician who rose to command the New Model Army in the Civil Wars against Charles I and supported the king's execution in…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oliver-goldsmith"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/oliver-goldsmith.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Oliver Goldsmith</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Oliver Goldsmith was an Irish writer, educated at Trinity College Dublin, who made his career in London as a member of Samuel Johnson's circle.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olivier-de-clisson"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olivier-de-clisson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olivier de Clisson</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Olivier de Clisson was a Breton soldier who fought first for John of Montfort, losing an eye at Auray in 1364, and then for France.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/oliwa-cathedral"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/oliwa-cathedral.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"