an><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Olmecs were the earliest major civilisation of Mesoamerica, flourishing in the Gulf Coast lowlands of southern Veracruz and Tabasco in Mexico from about 1200 to 400…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olof-skotkonung"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olof-skotkonung.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olof Skötkonung</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Olof Skötkonung was king of Sweden from about 995 and the first Swedish king known to have been a Christian, traditionally baptised at Husaby.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olof-tratalja"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olof-tratalja.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olof Trätälja</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Olof Trätälja, 'the Tree-Feller', is a legendary Swedish king of the Yngling line known from Ynglingatal and Snorri Sturluson's Ynglinga saga.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olomouc"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olomouc.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olomouc</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Olomouc is a city in central Moravia in the Czech Republic, on the Morava river.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/olosega"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/olosega.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Olosega</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Olosega is a small volcanic island in the Manuʻa group of American Samoa, linked to neighbouring Ofu by a bridge across a narrow channel.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/olous"><span class="enc-name">Olous</spa